# Agent Context Protocol

Use `.agent/` as durable project memory. Keep it concise; treat it as a map, not proof. Verify source before critical edits.

## Startup

- Missing `.agent/`: run `/bootstrap-context` before substantive work.
- Existing `.agent/`: use `sessionStart` summary, then read `HANDOFF.md`, `PROGRESS.md`, and only needed files.

## Ownership

| File | Owns |
|------|------|
| `.agent/HANDOFF.md` | Current task: status, next action, touched files, latest validation, blockers |
| `.agent/PROGRESS.md` | Rolling ledger: focus, done, in progress, backlog, blockers, last sync |
| `.agent/ARCHITECTURE.md` | Project map, entry points, boundaries, data flow, terms |
| `.agent/COMMANDS.md` | Commands, validation profile, slow/flaky notes, command-specific failure modes |
| `.agent/CONFIG.md` | Env names, secret locations, services, setup paths; never values |
| `.agent/CONVENTIONS.md` | Style, workflow, preferences, boundaries, review habits |
| `.agent/MEMORY.md` | Decisions, lessons, failed assumptions, bug roots, reusable fixes |

One owner per fact. Do not duplicate; add pointers only when useful.

## Update Triggers

- Start/pause/block/validate/substantial edit -> rewrite `HANDOFF.md`.
- Start/finish work, backlog, blockers -> update `PROGRESS.md`.
- Commands/checks -> `COMMANDS.md`.
- Preferences/conventions -> `CONVENTIONS.md`.
- Decisions/failures/lessons -> `MEMORY.md`.
- Architecture/terms -> `ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Safety

Ask before core behavior changes, architecture choices, critical config edits, irreversible operations, or unclear intent.
Keep edits surgical: every changed line must trace to the request or resulting cleanup. Mention unrelated issues; do not fix them unless asked.
Do not guess behavior, invent commands, skip checks, or claim completion without validation. Use `COMMANDS.md` for checks. Store latest results in `HANDOFF.md`, reusable rules in `COMMANDS.md`.
Never store secret values.

## Hygiene

- `HANDOFF.md` is a current snapshot, not a log. Rewrite it. Next action must be concrete and verifiable, preferably naming a `COMMANDS.md` check.
- `PROGRESS.md` is a rolling ledger; compact old work.
- `MEMORY.md` stores reusable lessons, not transcripts; consolidate repeats.
- Remove stale handoff details when there is no active task.
- End meaningful work with accurate `HANDOFF.md` and `PROGRESS.md`.
